    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-c, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6116\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to\ndesignating a portion of the state highway system as the \"Sergeant\nOmar G. Blowers Memorial Highway\"\n\nPurpose:  This bill designates a portion of State Route 70, from the\nCanaseraga village line to the Livingston County line, as the\n\"Sergeant Omar G.  Blowers Memorial Highway\".\n\nSummary of Provisions:  Highway law is amended adding a new section\n344-c to read as follows:  Portion of the state highway system to be\ndesignated as the \"Sergeant Omar G. Blowers Memorial Highway\".\n\nJustification:  This legislation will memorialize the sacrifice and\nselfless service of Sergeant Omar G. Blowers, who lost his life at the\nage of 19 serving in the United States Army during the Korean War.\n\nSergeant Blowers was taken prisoner in South Korea while fighting\nChinese military forces. He lost his life on May 30, 1951 after being\nheld prisoner for 107 days.\n\nThis legislation serves to honor his memory by designating the portion\nof State Route 70 which runs through his hometown of Swain, New York,\nas the \"Sergeant Omar G. Blowers Memorial Highway\".  Resolutions in\nsupport of this legislation have been passed by both the town of Burns\nand Allegany County.\n\nLegislative History: New Bill.\n\nFiscal Implications: None.\n\nEffective Date:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
